; Anomaly Coop - crafting, cooking, disassembly and inventory helpers of the local player: Keep Crafting Window Opened
; (zz_item_cooking_ / zz_ui_workshop_keep_crafting_window_open), Repair Notifications (item_parts_repair_notifications,
; zzzz_arti_jamming_repairs_repair_notifications), Unusable Parts Handler, Auto-Stacking Items (zatura_autostack),
; Workshop Parts Inventory (zone_keeper). Read after every coop_route*.ltx (coop_route.ltx explains the order), so it
; wins over the generated coop_route_gamma.ltx.
;
; The generator made all of them host (Ruling F2-29) because they create or release items. They are UI of the
; player's own inventory, and every one of them patches an owner or view module at file level (item_cooking.UICook,
; ui_workshop.UIWorkshop*, item_parts.disassembly_*, zzzz_arti_jamming_repairs, ui_inventory.UIInventory, ui_item), so
; the patched methods run on a client whatever the domain says. What the domain decides is their callbacks and their
; time events, and a time event follows the script of its function:
;   - the patched stock method creates a timer with a function of the patch file (the crafting windows refresh through
;     CreateTimeEvent(..., self.UpdateUi) / self.CollectValidItems; disassembly through timer_disassembly_item /
;     timer_disassembly_weapon / timer_disassembly_outfit). Host-only, the router removes the timer on a client:
;     the crafting window never refreshed, and a disassembly discarded the item (utils_item.discharge, a request) and
;     never gave the parts back: the item was lost.
;   - GUI_on_show / actor_on_item_take / on_option_change (unusable_parts_handler, zatura_autostack, zone_keeper) did
;     not run, so the window helpers worked on the host only.
; Owner: every machine runs the crafting of its own player.
;
; Except the refresh timers of the two keep-crafting-window mods (B3 review C3, pairs below). After a cook, craft,
; repair or upgrade their 0.1 s timer (self.UpdateUi, a function of the patch file) refreshes the window from the
; LOCAL inventory, where the ingredients just released stay until the host's EntityDestroy (a release on a client is
; a request, coop_requests.cpp client_destroy): the button came back on and a second action was free (the releases
; found nothing, the product was created again). Host-only, a client gets no refresh timer, and
; scripts\coop_mods_guard.script closes the window after the action on a client, as the stock windows do (a click on
; the meal list would otherwise re-enable the cook button from the window's stale item list). The cooking window's
; Reset timer (kit uses in the title) goes too: cosmetic.
;
; World calls on a client (call router, F2 T12): creating a result in the own inventory (alife_create_item(.., db.actor),
; alife_create(.., npc:id(), false) + alife():register for the parts of a disassembly) is a request to the host;
; alife_release of an own item is a request too (nil results, none is used). A result that belongs into a workshop
; stash (zz_ui_workshop_keep_crafting_window_open: stash_obj as the parent) is the stash's, not the player's, so the
; router refuses it (logged): a client's complex crafting at a workshop with a stash loses its product until F2 T12b.

[route_scripts]
zz_item_cooking_keep_crafting_window_open = owner
zz_ui_workshop_keep_crafting_window_open = owner
item_parts_repair_notifications = owner
zzzz_arti_jamming_repairs_repair_notifications = owner
unusable_parts_handler = owner
zatura_autostack = owner
zone_keeper = owner

[route_pairs]
time_event@zz_item_cooking_keep_crafting_window_open = host
time_event@zz_ui_workshop_keep_crafting_window_open = host
